{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1736","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1736","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1736\",\"parent_revision\":\"51a8e8362dc46f80390024e2ff8587a883e645cd2518e82c8f43a5c363c64f37\",\"root_revision\":\"51a8e8362dc46f80390024e2ff8587a883e645cd2518e82c8f43a5c363c64f37\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **replace filesystem-count plan_id generation with uuid-derived ids** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered during PR #1725 review \u2014 plan_id durability analysis\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`_next_plan_number` in `sam_schema/core/query.py` derives the next plan ID by counting `P*.yaml` files in the local plan directory. The memory backend resets `_next_plan_num = 1` on every server restart.\\n\\nThis means plan IDs (`P001`, `P002`, ...) restart from `P001` whenever:\\n- The `~/.dh/` state directory is wiped\\n- A CI runner starts fresh\\n- Tests run with `DH_STATE_HOME` pointing at a temp dir\\n- A new machine is provisioned\\n\\nWhen the counter resets, newly created plans get IDs that collide with plans already recorded in GitHub Issues, artifact manifests, and dispatch plans from prior runs. The `plan_id` durability fix in PR #1725 makes stored IDs survive reads, but does not fix the minting step \u2014 a wiped directory still produces `P001` again.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behaviour\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPlan IDs must be globally unique regardless of filesystem state. They must not collide across machines, CI environments, or after state directory wipes.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reference\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBeads (`bd`) addresses this identically: IDs are derived from `uuid4()` and shortened to a hash prefix (`bd-a1b2`). The ID is minted once at creation time and never re-derived from storage layout.\\n\\nSee `research/task-management/beads.md` for the beads ID scheme.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Affected Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 `_next_plan_number()`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` \u2014 `_next_plan_num` counter\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 uses `_next_plan_number` indirectly via `create_plan`\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b18503025af07a41b11992c2d969fbc75dc8b0340fc4bda410e21dcf1792b124\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVV9WRw\"}"}